1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:02,341
Before ChatGPT took the world by storm,

2
00:00:02,741 --> 00:00:04,482
the team behind its future rival made a

3
00:00:04,522 --> 00:00:07,724
surprising choice: they held their own
chatbot back.

4
00:00:08,644 --> 00:00:10,205
One of them was Dario Amodei.

5
00:00:10,725 --> 00:00:12,806
He had worked on AI models at OpenAI,

6
00:00:13,106 --> 00:00:15,087
then left and co-founded a new company:

7
00:00:15,487 --> 00:00:18,429
Anthropic. As his team developed an early
version

8
00:00:18,449 --> 00:00:20,650
of Claude, they worried that releasing it
could

9
00:00:20,690 --> 00:00:21,750
spark an AI race.

10
00:00:22,390 --> 00:00:24,191
If companies rushed to outdo one another,

11
00:00:24,551 --> 00:00:26,212
would they have enough time to make
powerful

12
00:00:26,272 --> 00:00:29,034
systems safe? So Anthropic waited.

13
00:00:29,654 --> 00:00:31,415
Then, in November 2022,

14
00:00:31,915 --> 00:00:34,176
OpenAI released ChatGPT to the public.

15
00:00:34,716 --> 00:00:36,877
Anthropic introduced Claude the following
March.

16
00:00:37,578 --> 00:00:40,539
Years later, Amodei said waiting had
probably cost

17
00:00:40,599 --> 00:00:42,520
Anthropic the chance to lead in AI for

18
00:00:42,640 --> 00:00:43,400
everyday users.
